{"id": "EUVD-2026-80442", "enisaUuid": "9020eb98-939b-357e-afbb-ec7c74e28501", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Skip NVMe LS reject IOCB when FW not started\n\nqla_nvme_xmt_ls_rsp() bails out to the out: label when firmware is not\nstarted (!ha->flags.fw_started), but the out: path unconditionally calls\nqla_nvme_ls_reject_iocb(), which ends in qla2x00_start_iocbs() and an\nunconditional doorbell write to the request queue in-pointer register.\nThis rings the firmware doorbell and queues an IOCB that stopped or\nresetting firmware cannot consume, and touches MMIO during the reset/EEH\nwindow where fw_started is also clear.\n\nOnly emit the LS reject IOCB (and ring the doorbell) when fw_started is\nset; otherwise just clean up and return. The post-allocation failure\ncases (SRB alloc / qla2x00_start_sp() failure) run with firmware started\nand still send the reject. Apply the same guard to the reject emission\nin qla2xxx_process_purls_pkt().", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:35", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2935b730211c5c1433aa6101fa3b55df2b63869a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c1fc75dd3fb6b6414508fbdf7aeed0d757c9120", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac4b019ac07844d3f67ea5e48b1d982b2170d1a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9bfb56e2c1bda49d3c5442d824569d71eec07e2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f7e46ebffc5781aab3f1f5a5d4350addbb5833f4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3frv-hcwj-933c", "CVE-2026-89842"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0212f63e-0280-3106-a121-32513bb2bdc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <e9bfb56e2c1bda49d3c5442d824569d71eec07e2"}, {"id": "3feb8454-6e96-39c9-9777-762b6a0d631c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <ac4b019ac07844d3f67ea5e48b1d982b2170d1a7"}, {"id": "54c5fa95-10b8-33e8-aa90-695982a188a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "6a456f4b-61f9-3bfe-b1a6-49a024243647", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <2935b730211c5c1433aa6101fa3b55df2b63869a"}, {"id": "80257be2-2e49-3af6-9b0a-a29db5f0a6cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "841b4826-df29-35a3-b818-44865c73d787", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "848fb17b-8dc0-3d45-b896-ca3b456e5e98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a665f3ad-b0d5-3be2-a7c8-ee8e7699b6d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c5255eef-05d2-3e2e-a1e0-95124b69eef4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "d7bba084-ec40-33b0-aefc-4f8ca97b1e4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <7c1fc75dd3fb6b6414508fbdf7aeed0d757c9120"}, {"id": "f5446efc-19ec-37df-a087-50b7cffaaabe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "875386b98857822b77ac7f95bdf367b70af5b78c <f7e46ebffc5781aab3f1f5a5d4350addbb5833f4"}, {"id": "f8efa052-e72f-3afa-8200-061edf469c75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "78e75aa9-9842-38ba-9823-4f54f8e03533", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}